;;; `naf-upward-closure.ein` again: the probe of a program on which `dead`
;;; is not upward-closed under `absent`.
;;;
;;; Below this header the program is `../naf-upward-closure.ein`'s, its `:why`
;;; texts aside. That file's header is the argument.
;;;
;;; ── What is said of it ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `bad` concludes `(false)` from `(absent (q ?x))` over `q`, which a
;;; commitment can still extend: a node that holds `(p A)` without `(q A)`
;;; matches `bad`, and one that holds both does not. The static check flags
;;; the program. It loads, every command answers it with the warning that
;;; it is not monotone, and nothing is claimed of its answer (Q-M1f.564).
;;; The file states no claim.
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;;
